-- title:
--   Gluing Xi from local transports: existence, leg, naturality
-- statement:
--   Let $r,\bar r$ be primes with $\bar r\neq r$ and $N\ge 1$ with $r\nmid N$; let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for the $\pi$-adic topology of an irreducible $\pi$, with $\#(\mathcal O/\pi)=r$ and $(r)=(\pi)$, and $K_0$ a fraction field of $\mathcal O$; let $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ be a characteristic-zero domain over $\mathcal O$ with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal being maximal, such that every element satisfies a monic $\mathcal O$-polynomial modulo $\pi$, every monic polynomial of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$, and $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^r \pmod\pi$. Let $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ be indefinite and a division algebra exactly at the places above $r$ and $\bar r$, $\Lambda$ a maximal order containing $\mathbb Z$, and $\mathrm{coord}:\Lambda\to \mathbb W(\mathbb F_{r^2})^2$ an injective, additive, dense coordinatisation with the Frobenius-twisted multiplication rule, $\mathrm{coord}(1)=(1,0)$ and the trace condition. Further data: a fake elliptic curve $A_0$ with $\Lambda$-action and level $N$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ over it and formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of $A_0$ realising $A_0$ as a formal module via $\mathrm{coord}$ and $X_0$; a ring map $\iota:\mathbb W(\mathbb F_{r^2})\to O^{\mathrm{nr}}$; a special formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ of height $4$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/r$; a moduli package $M$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ which is a Zariski sheaf, together with $\eta$ sending rigidified objects over $B$ to points of $M(B)$ and the three assumptions on $\eta$ (it separates admissible rigidified objects exactly up to the isomorphism relation, it commutes with base change, and every point of $M(B)$ comes, locally on a finite Zariski cover of $B$ by localisations, from an admissible rigidified object); an injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $\mathbb W(\mathbb F_{r^2})$-action and $\varpi$ on $\Phi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ whose image is commensurable with $M_2(\mathcal O)$ up to a fixed power of $r$; and finally $\kappa:O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi\to O^{\mathrm{nr}}/r$ compatible with the quotient maps, together with an isogeny $\beta_0$ of height $4n_0$ from $\Phi$ to $\kappa_*X_0$. The assertion is that there is an assignment $\Xi$ which, for every Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$, every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi:O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to B$ and every proof that $\pi$ is nilpotent in $B$, sends a rigidified curve $x=(E,\rho)$ over $(B,\psi)$ — a fake elliptic curve $E$ over $B$ with level $N$ and $\Lambda$-action, together with a rigidification of $E$ relative to $A_0$ — to a point of $M$ over $B$ in the sense of `ModuliPackage.GPoint`, i.e. a triple consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to B$, nilpotence of $r$ in $B$ and a point of $M$ over it, subject to three conditions. First, if $B$ has no idempotents other than $0$ and $1$, the leg of $\Xi B\,\psi\,h_B\,x$ is $\psi\circ\mathrm{Fr}^k$ for some $k\in\mathbb Z$. Second, for $\varphi:B\to B'$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra map, rigidified curves $x$ over $(B,\psi)$ and $x'$ over $(B',\varphi\circ\psi)$ and $g:x'_1.A\to x_1.A$ exhibiting the curve of $x'$ as pullback of that of $x$ along $\varphi$ and the rigidification of $x'$ as pullback of that of $x$, one has $\Xi B'\,(\varphi\circ\psi)\,h_{B'}\,x' = (\Xi B\,\psi\,h_B\,x).\mathrm{map}\,\varphi$. Third, if moreover $B$ has only the trivial idempotents, $r$ is nilpotent in $B$, and $X,\theta$ realise the curve of $x$ as a formal module via $\mathrm{coord}$, then there are $j\le 1$ and a rigidified object $t$ over $B$ with $t.X=X$, which is a rig transport of the rigidification of $x$ with respect to $\theta_0,\kappa,\beta_0,\theta$ and $j$, is admissible for $\iota$ and $\psi\circ\mathrm{Fr}^{-j}$, and satisfies $\Xi B\,\psi\,h_B\,x = \langle \psi\circ\mathrm{Fr}^{-j},\,h_{Br},\,\eta\,B\,(\psi\circ\mathrm{Fr}^{-j})\,h_{Br}\,t\rangle$.
--
--   This is the gluing step in the construction of the Čerednik–Drinfeld dictionary sending a rigidified fake elliptic curve over a base in which $\pi$ is nilpotent to a point of the moduli package attached to the special formal module $\Phi$: the three clauses record the Frobenius leg of the resulting point over a connected base, its naturality under base change, and its defining description in terms of rig transports on a base carrying formal coordinates. It is used by the companion statement [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.exists_rigidifiedToG_natural_isRigTransport`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.exists_rigidifiedToG_natural_isRigTransport), which adds the clause comparing $\Xi$ on isomorphic rigidified curves.
